---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Tooltip from '@components/Tooltip.astro'
import meIcon from '@assets/me.png'
import { localePaths } from '@i18n/utils'
import { SITE } from '@src/config.ts'

// One file, every locale.
export const getStaticPaths = localePaths
---

<BaseLayout width="narrow" title="About me" description="Who I am and what I work on.">
  <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
    <Image
      src={meIcon}
      alt=""
      width={36}
      densities={[1, 2]}
      class="size-9 shrink-0 object-contain"
      loading="eager"
    />
    <h1 class="page-title text-ink-strong">About me</h1>
  </div>

  <div class="prose mt-6">
    <p>
      Hi, I'm Josh! Welcome to my digital workshop where I tinker on projects
      and begin my journey of leaving a mark on the software community. I love
      all aspects of the engineering lifecycle from QA, security, software and
      of course platform engineering. I am currently working at <a href="https://www.crunchyroll.com">Crunchyroll</a> as a
      Core Infrastructure engineer where I build reusable infrastructure
      components, CI/CD workflows and provide support to the beloved engineering
      teams so they can bring their services to life. This could mean I'm spending
      my day debugging network issues in aws, IaC drift headaches, deploying new
      services, deprecating old ones or building some cool automation or
      internal service so that I can make someone else's headache a process they enjoy.
    </p>

    <p>
      I created this site because as I get further into my career I want a place
      to record the projects I have created and the problems I solve along the
      way, as well as transcribe my thoughts and opinions so I have a history to
      look back on as they change and I get better as an engineer. I'm not sure
      who may read them in the day of AI, but maybe they'll provide some benefit to
      another engineer querying an AI CLI tool on how to solve a similar issue. (cmon that had to get a laugh)
    </p>

    <p>
      I spend a lot of time on personal projects and attempting to teach myself
      Afrikaans, <Tooltip label="I get better every day" focusable underline
        ><em>ek word elke dag beter</em></Tooltip
      >, but when I am not doing
      either of those I am enjoying a good workout, watching F1, playing video games, reading
      the Bible or spending time with my wife and dog Maple who only wants to
      play fetch inside the house!
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>

    <p>Dont be shy, I'd love to chat about anything software related, your struggles or insights with learning a second language or if you just want to connect! </p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Email</strong>:{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.links.email}`}>{SITE.links.email}</a>
      </li>
      <li><a href={SITE.links.github}>GitHub</a></li>
      <li><a href={SITE.links.linkedIn}>LinkedIn</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What I'm doing now</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>Working full time.</li>
      <li>Playing around with my personal website.</li>
      <li>
        Iterating on <a href="https://lawademy.com">Lawademy</a> as we keep
        building out outlines for law students.
      </li>
      <li>Starting my blogging journey.</li>
      <li>Forgetting my Afrikaans SVO grammar structure.</li>
      <li>Attempting to keep up with the AI craze.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Faith</h2>

    <p>Currently reading through:</p>

    <p>
      <strong
        ><a href="https://www.bibleref.com/Judges/1/Judges-chapter-1.html"
          >Judges</a
        ></strong
      > — the Israelites are fully committed to the goldfish memory bit, and not
      in a good way.
    </p>

    <h2>Learning Afrikaans</h2>

    <p>
      I'm teaching myself Afrikaans. These are the resources doing the heavy
      lifting, roughly in the order I reach for them:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="https://app.talkpal.ai/">TalkPal</a> — interactive audio and
        speech practice. The closest thing to a conversation partner on demand.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          href="https://theswissbay.ch/pdf/Books/Linguistics/Mega%20linguistics%20pack/Indo-European/Germanic/Afrikaans%2C%20Teach%20Yourself%20%28McDermott%29.pdf"
          >Teach Yourself Afrikaans</a
        > (McDermott) — vocabulary, grammar, and reading.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://library.teachyourself.com/">Teach Yourself library</a> —
        audio courses to listen along with.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://open.spotify.com/show/5cnUg6FSfG3fdjfzA86m8c">KLETS</a>
        — an Afrikaans podcast, for real-world listening at real-world speed.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      And if you don't have someone in your life to speak it with, get a tutor
      from the country. Nothing replaces an actual conversation.
    </p>

    <h2>Miscellaneous</h2>

    <p>If you're after the short version, here's my <a href="/resume/">resume</a>.</p>
  </div>

</BaseLayout>
